Finally, after almost two months of playing, I also beat Slash'EM.
Here's how:

Started the usual Mon-Dop-Fem-Cha, since I was told they were the easiest.
Everything was quite straightforwarded, no special starting equipment and no marker.
Went straight down the mines to get to XL 9 for polycontrol (the most important
thing for a Doppelganger). Minetown altar was crossaligned (as usual...) and
Izchak had two magic lamps which I couldn't afford at the moment.
Went on to mines end which was NOT the haunted library for a change. I get that
one on three out of four games or so...
Finished mines end, identified a luckstone on the way by kicking and trying to
#name it "The Heart of Ahriman".
Reached XL 9 and immediately polymorphed into a crystal golem. 300 HP and a
random breath weapon sure are handy :)
While I was at it, I also cleaned out the level below mines end for two
healthstones.
Used all the gems to identify my loot at the friendly general store shopkeeper
and bought the two magic lamps. Uncursed. Too bad I have no altar yet.
Okay, went on and set up a stash at Dlvl 6. It will stay there for the rest of
the game.
Next was - obviously - Sokoban which yielded a nice amulet of reflection.
Picked up a bag of holding along the way which was identified by trying to #name
it "Wallet of Perseus". Ironically, I didn't get that one later on.

My first altar outside of minetown was then on the quest home level, which I
converted and used to pray for some holy water.

Around this point I decided to try the famed gypsy farming. I blessed the lamps
and wished for two cursed scrolls of genocide.
Since sacfesting was not possible at the quest home level, I also wished for the
blessed fixed +3 Gauntlets of Defense, and got them.
Okay, so I got myself a nice, lit mine level and reverse genocided my first
bunch of gypsies. Got five, nice. (C)alled them 1 through 5 and started playing
Three Card Monte.
Three days later I had racked up 32 wishes.
I used the incubi for leveling, and otherwise wished up the usual ascension kit
stuff. Helm of Brilliance, several markers in varying BUC states, CoMR and so on.

Feeling strong enough at experience level 30 and over 300 HP and PW I went to
put my monk to the first test: Vecna.
He went down like a brick in water.
For guys like him I used the following chained blitz:
Chii Strike - pummel - pummel - pummel - ground slam
I never saw the ground slam even once.

With hungerless regeneration I went on to the Beholder who killed himself using
a death gaze and my amulet.
To complete the hattrick, I also got the Nighthorn from the lawful quest, but
not before genociding the whole 'h' class.
Oh, and asphynxes. In earlier Mon-Dop games I accidentally bit one as a Vampire...

Being confident about myself, I started the quest.
Kaen did some fun-fair-level fire magic which didn't really bother me and went
down to the above mentioned chained blitz without taking a single hitpoint from me.

Astral vision, YEAH!

Then, nothing interesting happened for some time.
Found a random WoW at (0:3) and felt mocked.
Got the castle WoW at (0:3) and felt even more so.
Even got a wish from the throne in Grund's Stronghold.

Reached Medusa then.
And of course I had no levitation with me.
Used my telecontrol and a cursed scroll of tele to get me back to my stash on
level 6 and got my ring of levitation and some cursed scrolls of teleport.
Same way back to Medusa...
Medusa stoned herself and Perseus only had his damn shield.

After Medusa I got two iron-bar maze-levels which aren't quite as scare to a
doppelganger as to other races (probably).

Castle fell easily by the back door.

Anyway, VotD was quite different. Being dumped into its middle rather than near
the stairs is nasty. And Vampire Mages are, too.
Anyway, got my way through there without much hassle.

Sooo, the fabled Slash'EM Gehennom lay before me.

The varying Demons were just as boring as the ones in vanilla with the (noble?)
exception of Demogorgon.
Having never met him in vanilla, I had no experience with him.
And him being on a bones file and right next to the upstairs didn't really help
either.
Anyway, chained blitz as above also did him in, but not before taking 150 HP off
me within 2 rounds and sickening me. Ouch.
That's where my blessed +6 unicorn horn came handy. But it took two tries and
that got me _really_ worried.

The bones yielded the +6 Bat from Hell, a 1:0 WoW and some gems and other minor
stuff, nothing really useful.

The vibrating square was found on Dlvl 62. Back to Rodney, introducing him to
one of my three wands of death and off I go.

Done the invocation and using my trusty ring of conflict, even the Sanctum was easy.
Got the amulet, #name'd it and run like the devil was after me.

Turned out, he wasn't. Rodney didn't appear and I didn't even get a "mysterious
force" holding me back. I feel cheated...

Stopped on my stash to quaff all those healing potions for >400 HP, just in case
and taking some other stuff with me.
My weight then was 996/1000. Being a pack rat/score whore crossover is baaad.

Ran up to the Planes.
Offed Rodney again, confused myself and read a scroll of gold detection.
After that the whole planes took less than 5 minutes.

On Astral I put my conflict ring back on (in addition to a ring of free action),
wished for a blessed fixed +7 greased partly eaten cockatrice corpse and whacked
my way to the right. Pestilence waited there whom I introduced to a wand of death.
Ran to the high altar, which was lawful. Me being chaotic, I got a helm of
opposite alignment out of the bag of holding, put it on and #offer'ed the amulet.
You are bathed in radiance...


blindcoder, lawful female doppelganger Monk






